WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.629
So far GROUP BY has produced one summary grain at a
time

00:00:04.566 --> 00:00:10.669
Advanced grouping features let one query produce
several summary levels GROUPING

00:00:10.695 --> 00:00:16.548
SETS lets you explicitly list the summary
combinations you want ROLLUP

00:00:16.561 --> 00:00:20.917
is useful for hierarchical reports such as category
then product then a

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:27.061
grand total CUBE generates every grouping
combination of the listed dimensions

00:00:28.799 --> 00:00:32.746
These features reduce the need to write several
separate aggregation queries and

00:00:32.772 --> 00:00:38.580
combine them manually The tradeoff is that the
output contains different grains

00:00:38.606 --> 00:00:42.780
in the same result That means you must understand
what each row

00:00:42.793 --> 00:00:48.454
represents and how subtotal placeholders are
displayed We will use a small

00:00:48.467 --> 00:00:51.414
product-sales table so you can see those levels
clearly
